.Dd July 18, 2026
.Dt TARFS 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm tarfs
.Nd read-only tar archive file system
.Sh SYNOPSIS
To load the driver as a module at boot time, place the following line in
.Xr loader.conf 5 :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
tarfs_load="YES"
.Ed
.Pp
Alternatively, load it on demand:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
kldload tarfs
.Ed
.Pp
To mount a tar archive:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
mount -t tarfs /path/to/archive.tar /mnt
.Ed
.Pp
or with the helper:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
mount_tarfs /path/to/archive.tar /mnt
.Ed
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
file system presents a POSIX ustar archive
.Pq with optional PAX extensions
as a read-only directory tree.
The archive is scanned at mount time to build an in-memory directory
index; file contents are read from the backing archive on demand.
.Pp
Supported member types include regular files, directories, symbolic
links, hard links to regular files, character and block devices, and
FIFOs.
Device and FIFO nodes are visible in the name space and via
.Xr stat 2
type bits; opening them returns
.Er EOPNOTSUPP
.Pq design freeze: metadata display only .
.Pp
GNU sparse format 1.0
.Pq PAX keys GNU.sparse.*
is supported: the logical file size is
.Va GNU.sparse.realsize ,
holes read as zero, and mapped extents supply data.
.Pp
A subset of
.Va SCHILY.fflags
.Pq for example Cm nodump , Cm uchg
is mapped into
.Vt va_flags .
.Sh OPTIONS
.Nm
accepts standard mount options that apply to read-only file systems
.Pq see
.Xr mount 8 .
The file system is always mounted read-only.
.Sh COMPRESSION
POSIX ustar/PAX archives may be compressed with
.Xr zstd 1 .
gzip and xz remain unsupported
.Pq same as FreeBSD tarfs for gzip/xz; FreeBSD also supports zstd .
.Pp
Example:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
mount_tarfs archive.tar.zst /mnt
.Ed
.Pp
For best random-read performance on large zstd archives, build multi-frame
streams
.Pq e.g. bsdtar zstd:frame-per-file / zstd:max-frame-size .
.Sh IMPLEMENTATION NOTES
.Bl -bullet
.It
Lookup uses DragonFly namecache
.Fn vop_nresolve
/
.Fn vop_nlookupdotdot ,
not FreeBSD cached lookup.
.It
There is no vfs_hash index; vnodes are allocated from the per-mount node table.
.It
Hard-link members resolve to the target regular-file node
.Pq FreeBSD-style follow .
.It
On
.Dx ,
.Vt st_rdev
for character/block nodes comes from an attached cdev.
Archive device nodes never open a real device, so
.Xr stat 1
.Cm %Hr / %Lr
report NOUDEV;
.Vt va_rmajor
/
.Vt va_rminor
are still filled from the archive for VFS consumers.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Load the module and mount a tree fixture:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
kldload tarfs
mkdir -p /mnt/tar
mount_tarfs /data/fixtures/tree.tar /mnt/tar
find /mnt/tar -ls
umount /mnt/tar
.Ed
.Pp
Pre-extract zstd then mount:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
zstd -d /data/fixtures/hello.tar.zst -o /tmp/hello.tar
mount_tarfs /tmp/hello.tar /mnt/tar
cat /mnt/tar/hello.txt
umount /mnt/tar
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr tar 1 ,
.Xr mount 2 ,
.Xr stat 2 ,
.Xr loader.conf 5 ,
.Xr mount 8 ,
.Xr mount_tarfs 8

.Sh COMPATIBILITY
This port aims for FreeBSD
.Nm
semantic parity where practical on DragonFly:
read-only ustar/PAX, GNU sparse 1.0, SCHILY.fflags, device/FIFO metadata,
and zstd compression.  Additional FreeBSD-aligned interfaces include
.Xr mount 8
options
.Cm uid , Cm gid , Cm mode , Cm as ,
NFS file-handle conversion
.Pq vfs_vget / fhtovp / vptofh ,
buffer strategy
.Pq vop_bmap / vop_strategy ,
and
.Xr sysctl 8
node
.Va vfs.tarfs.zio .
gzip and xz remain unsupported.
.Sh HISTORY
.Nm
originated in
.Fx
as a read-only archive file system.
This page documents the
.Dx
port under
.Pa sys/vfs/tarfs .
.Sh AUTHORS
.An -nosplit
The FreeBSD
.Nm
implementation was developed by Juniper Networks, Inc. and Klara, Inc.
The DragonFly port and this manual page were written for the
.Dx
project.
.Sh BUGS
Large archives allocate metadata for every member at mount time; memory
and mount latency scale with member count.
.Pp
Memory-mapped I/O
.Pq VMIO
and kernel zstd are not implemented.
